<!-- ── FAQ ── -->
<section style="background:var(--cream-d);padding:72px 48px;">
  <div style="max-width:800px;margin:0 auto;">
    <div class="stag-o">Common Questions</div>
    <h2 class="sh-o" style="margin-bottom:40px;">Quick answers.<br/><em>No runaround.</em></h2>
    <div style="display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:0;">

      <details style="border-bottom:1px solid rgba(139,34,0,0.1);padding:20px 0;" open>
        <summary style="font-size:1rem;font-weight:800;color:var(--dark);cursor:pointer;list-style:none;display:flex;justify-content:space-between;align-items:center;">
          Do you serve my area?
          <span style="color:var(--orange);font-size:1.2rem;font-weight:400;">+</span>
        </summary>
        <p style="margin-top:14px;font-size:0.9rem;line-height:1.75;color:#7A4020;font-weight:400;">We're Texas-based and currently expanding our coverage footprint. The best way to find out is to reach out — we'll tell you straight whether we can serve you today or when we expect to be in your area.</p>
      </details>

      <details style="border-bottom:1px solid rgba(139,34,0,0.1);padding:20px 0;">
        <summary style="font-size:1rem;font-weight:800;color:var(--dark);cursor:pointer;list-style:none;display:flex;justify-content:space-between;align-items:center;">
          How fast is installation?
          <span style="color:var(--orange);font-size:1.2rem;font-weight:400;">+</span>
        </summary>
        <p style="margin-top:14px;font-size:0.9rem;line-height:1.75;color:#7A4020;font-weight:400;">Wireless deployments typically go up in days, not months. No trenching, no waiting on contractors. Hardened Ethernet runs take a little longer depending on your space — we'll give you a realistic timeline upfront.</p>
      </details>

      <details style="border-bottom:1px solid rgba(139,34,0,0.1);padding:20px 0;">
        <summary style="font-size:1rem;font-weight:800;color:var(--dark);cursor:pointer;list-style:none;display:flex;justify-content:space-between;align-items:center;">
          Are there contracts or data caps?
          <span style="color:var(--orange);font-size:1.2rem;font-weight:400;">+</span>
        </summary>
        <p style="margin-top:14px;font-size:0.9rem;line-height:1.75;color:#7A4020;font-weight:400;">No data caps. Ever. No throttling. No selling your traffic data to advertisers. We're an independent ISP — your traffic belongs to you, not our marketing partners. On contracts: month-to-month is our default. We'd rather earn your business every month than trap you in a 3-year agreement like the big guys do.</p>
      </details>

      <details style="border-bottom:1px solid rgba(139,34,0,0.1);padding:20px 0;">
        <summary style="font-size:1rem;font-weight:800;color:var(--dark);cursor:pointer;list-style:none;display:flex;justify-content:space-between;align-items:center;">
          What happens when something breaks?
          <span style="color:var(--orange);font-size:1.2rem;font-weight:400;">+</span>
        </summary>
        <p style="margin-top:14px;font-size:0.9rem;line-height:1.75;color:#7A4020;font-weight:400;">You call or text <strong style="color:var(--dark)">(512) 200-4744</strong>. A real human answers who already knows your setup — not a bot, not a queue, not someone reading from a script. We don't hide behind a portal. We're accountable the old-fashioned way: you have our number.</p>
      </details>

      <details style="padding:20px 0;">
        <summary style="font-size:1rem;font-weight:800;color:var(--dark);cursor:pointer;list-style:none;display:flex;justify-content:space-between;align-items:center;">
          Can you handle everything — internet AND the local network?
          <span style="color:var(--orange);font-size:1.2rem;font-weight:400;">+</span>
        </summary>
        <p style="margin-top:14px;font-size:0.9rem;line-height:1.75;color:#7A4020;font-weight:400;">Yes — that's exactly the point. Most businesses deal with their ISP for internet and a separate IT company for everything else, and nobody talks to each other. HowdyNET owns the whole stack. One call, one invoice, one team that's accountable for all of it.</p>
      </details>
          <details class="faq-item">
            <summary class="faq-q">Do I have to change my ISP to use RanchHand™?</summary>
            <p style="margin-top:14px;font-size:0.9rem;line-height:1.75;color:#7A4020;font-weight:400;">Nope. That's kind of the whole point. RanchHand™ works with Comcast, AT&T, Spectrum, or any ISP you're currently using — or stuck with. We plug our managed gateway appliance between your existing modem and your network. Your ISP doesn't even know we're there. You just get a dramatically better network experience without changing a thing on your ISP side.</p>
          </details>
          <details class="faq-item">
            <summary class="faq-q">What's the deal with the RanchHand™ hardware — do I own it?</summary>
            <p style="margin-top:14px;font-size:0.9rem;line-height:1.75;color:#7A4020;font-weight:400;">Two options, honest math: <strong>Month-to-month</strong> at $79/mo with a $199 hardware deposit — cancel anytime, deposit refunded within 90 days if you return the hardware in working condition. Or a <strong>12-month commitment</strong> at the same $79/mo with hardware included at no extra cost. The commitment covers our ROI on the appliance — same as how a phone carrier works. No surprises either way, because we just told you everything.</p>
          </details>
          <details class="faq-item">
            <summary class="faq-q">What exactly does RanchHand™ do that my current router doesn't?</summary>
            <p style="margin-top:14px;font-size:0.9rem;line-height:1.75;color:#7A4020;font-weight:400;">Quite a bit, actually. Your current router was probably set up once and never touched again. RanchHand™ is actively managed: we remediate bufferbloat (the #1 cause of choppy video calls), shape traffic so your POS and VoIP always get priority, block ads and unwanted content at the DNS level before they reach any device, build a behavioral fingerprint of your network and flag anything unusual, and give you a secure VPN so you're on your own network from anywhere. Oh — and we're watching it 24/7.</p>
          </details>
          <details class="faq-item">
            <summary class="faq-q">If I'm not in your ISP coverage area, can I still get HowdyNET?</summary>
            <p style="margin-top:14px;font-size:0.9rem;line-height:1.75;color:#7A4020;font-weight:400;">Absolutely — and that's exactly what RanchHand™ is for. S'pose you're on the edge of our coverage, or in a city we haven't expanded to yet — RanchHand™ gets you everything except the ISP connection itself. When we do expand to your area, upgrading to full HowdyNET internet is seamless. Join the coverage waitlist and you'll be first to know.</p>
          </details>
</div>
  </div>
</section>
